# The status log is append-only: many branches add lines at once, so keep both sides instead of a conflict (git's
# built-in union merge). The status page itself is one file per entry under wiki/status/, so two branches collide only
# on the same entry, and then as a real conflict (ADR-038).
wiki/STATUS_LOG.md merge=union
# docs/INDEX.md lists one row per document, and parallel branches add rows near each other; keep both sides
# (owner, 2026-11-25, ADR-036). build_docs_index.py --check fails on a row or intro left twice. Like the other drivers it
# runs in local merges only, not GitHub's merge button: merge origin/main into the branch locally when GitHub shows a conflict.
docs/INDEX.md merge=union
# The pipeline map's graph merges itself by node id and edge ends: tools/ops/merge_pipeline_map.py, set up by make wt
# and the session-start hook (--install). GitHub never runs this driver: merge origin/main into the branch locally.
# The two map pages built from it are not committed (ADR-036).
docs/pipeline-map/pipeline_map.json merge=pipeline-map
# The two ratchet lists hold one row per key, and parallel branches add rows near each other; keep both sides (owner,
# 2026-11-27, ADR-041). A row both sides edited comes out twice, and the loader stops on it as "listed twice"
# (hand_tables.csv by file and table, py_sizes.csv by path), so union never hides a real conflict.
tools/audit/hand_tables.csv merge=union
tools/audit/py_sizes.csv merge=union
